WEBVTT

00:08.050 --> 00:09.350
Almost.

00:11.880 --> 00:15.330
Put your left foot on that bulge there.

00:16.740 --> 00:17.500
That's it.

00:17.770 --> 00:19.510
Grab this branch.

00:24.680 --> 00:26.300
That hole.

00:26.700 --> 00:28.170
Face the other way.

00:32.530 --> 00:33.830
I made it!

00:33.830 --> 00:35.040
Congrats.

00:35.400 --> 00:36.520
Hey!

00:36.520 --> 00:39.630
No climbing where the grown-ups 
and familiars can't see you!

00:39.900 --> 00:41.150
Okay.

00:41.790 --> 00:44.300
You're such a good teacher.

00:44.300 --> 00:47.570
And you can climb faster than I can.

00:50.650 --> 00:53.260
That's not true.

02:46.890 --> 02:49.220
Have you two gotten used to College yet?

02:49.480 --> 02:54.440
Chise's a mage, and this is Zoe's
 first time going to school, right?

02:54.440 --> 02:55.930
Well...

02:57.420 --> 03:01.320
I'm still not used to being 
around so many people.

03:01.320 --> 03:02.130
Yeah.

03:02.420 --> 03:04.540
Other than that, it's fun.

03:04.540 --> 03:07.090
There's a lot of subjects I like, too.

03:07.730 --> 03:10.390
There's a bunch of different 
activities in P.E., too.

03:10.390 --> 03:11.140
Today's...

03:11.140 --> 03:12.330
Bouldering.

03:12.750 --> 03:16.650
We do a lot of P.E. so 
we're always ready to act.

03:16.970 --> 03:19.920
I'd rather study than exercise.

03:19.920 --> 03:21.350
Not that I'd enjoy either one.

03:21.350 --> 03:22.790
You there!

03:23.130 --> 03:26.340
Get a move on if you're done resting!

03:26.870 --> 03:27.920
I'm going.

03:28.350 --> 03:29.880
See you.

03:40.850 --> 03:42.310
That was impressive.

03:43.320 --> 03:44.800
Thanks.

03:49.760 --> 03:50.870
Down she goes.

03:53.160 --> 03:55.000
Are you all right, Lucy?

03:55.000 --> 03:57.110
Don't freak out like that.

03:57.110 --> 03:58.500
You'll make it look like a big deal.

03:59.390 --> 04:00.590
Sorry.

04:01.820 --> 04:03.940
Why do you keep...

04:05.120 --> 04:06.480
I'm fine.

04:06.480 --> 04:07.950
I'm not hurt.

04:07.950 --> 04:10.350
Your turn to go up and fall.

04:10.350 --> 04:11.300
Okay.

04:12.310 --> 04:14.770
Do you have any advice?

04:18.010 --> 04:19.620
Are you worried?

04:21.310 --> 04:25.320
You're watching her all the time 
when you don't have classes.

04:26.670 --> 04:27.780
You could see me, huh?

04:28.090 --> 04:32.530
I may not have much magic power, 
but my eyesight's decent enough.

04:34.000 --> 04:36.710
She makes faces here
that she doesn't show me.

04:37.500 --> 04:38.790
Does that upset you?

04:39.380 --> 04:42.120
I suppose it does.

04:42.900 --> 04:44.900
But I can't look away, either.

04:45.380 --> 04:47.760
I think I understand.

04:48.370 --> 04:49.210
You do?

04:50.030 --> 04:51.860
I do.

04:51.860 --> 04:54.790
I remember a lot of bad things,

04:54.790 --> 04:57.510
but good memories come 
with them at the same time.

04:57.910 --> 04:59.010
Something like that.

04:59.610 --> 05:02.480
So I can't help but reminisce.

05:03.210 --> 05:06.860
It doesn't make sense, but it happens.

05:08.830 --> 05:11.860
I see you making that face often lately.

05:12.560 --> 05:15.130
What are you thinking about?

05:17.320 --> 05:18.860
Well...

05:19.240 --> 05:21.660
Living for as long as I have, 
there's a lot to think about.

05:22.690 --> 05:26.430
But I often remember my hometown of Dresden.

05:26.810 --> 05:29.250
Dresden? Of Germany?

05:30.540 --> 05:32.550
It was a beautiful city.

05:33.990 --> 05:38.810
The River Elbe, with the linden 
trees along its banks...

05:40.670 --> 05:42.180
The corner bakery.

05:43.610 --> 05:45.680
The tailor's shop where I bought my coat.

05:47.060 --> 05:50.450
I left my home long before 
the war broke out.

05:51.060 --> 05:54.600
By the time I returned after it ended, 
there was nothing but rubble.

05:55.450 --> 05:58.050
Everything I remembered was buried.

05:58.660 --> 06:03.510
Once you lose everything, you 
remember all kinds of things.

06:08.310 --> 06:15.930
I still can't decide if such memories 
are a good thing or a bad thing.

06:16.530 --> 06:18.130
All you're doing is remembering.

06:18.930 --> 06:21.350
And it's not as though you 
can recall everything.

06:21.350 --> 06:26.160
It's too complicated to say if 
any one memory is good or bad.

06:26.670 --> 06:30.550
Perhaps if the experience isn't 
uncomfortable, then it's a good memory.

06:30.550 --> 06:32.900
Should it really be that simple?

06:32.900 --> 06:34.330
There isn't much more to it.

06:34.970 --> 06:39.330
You should try asking various people 
more of those types of questions.

06:39.860 --> 06:42.070
You'll hear all kinds of answers.

06:42.770 --> 06:45.340
That girl there is my master.

06:45.930 --> 06:49.200
I don't intend on asking others 
for their teachings too much.

06:50.620 --> 06:52.060
But I'll keep that in mind.

06:57.080 --> 06:59.200
<i>He doesn't seem malicious.</i>

06:59.200 --> 07:00.550
<i>Well, whatever.</i>

07:04.080 --> 07:07.750
<i>I was just chasing him down 
to give him some documents.</i>

07:08.600 --> 07:13.000
<i>No wonder his appearance hasn't 
changed much since I first met him.</i>

07:13.000 --> 07:16.020
<i>He's a mage of sorts.</i>

07:24.220 --> 07:26.770
You might be putting too much 
strength into your hold.

07:27.250 --> 07:30.020
It's important not to use more 
stamina than you need to.

07:30.020 --> 07:32.060
You've become friends with her, huh?

07:33.990 --> 07:35.390
I don't know.

07:35.390 --> 07:38.790
I know you're not good at talking to people.

07:39.240 --> 07:42.070
You should take this opportunity 
to talk to her more.

07:42.640 --> 07:43.770
Is that...

07:45.080 --> 07:46.570
Is that an order?

08:14.730 --> 08:18.450
There's nothing wrong with caring for 
others, but you'd best get to bed.

08:59.000 --> 09:02.420
<i>"I'm really sorry that I couldn't
 do the morning routine.</i>

09:02.420 --> 09:04.190
<i>I am going back to my house
 because I was called.</i>

09:04.190 --> 09:05.940
<i>I'll be back by tomorrow."</i>

09:05.940 --> 09:08.360
"I'll be back by tomorrow."

09:08.970 --> 09:10.530
Miss Veronica!

09:10.800 --> 09:12.790
Good morning, ma'am!

09:12.790 --> 09:14.240
Morning.

09:15.750 --> 09:18.830
I'll have to be ready to 
console her tomorrow.

09:45.260 --> 09:47.090
Welcome home, miss.

09:47.400 --> 09:48.670
I'm back.

09:52.150 --> 09:53.310
Where is Grandmother?

09:54.070 --> 09:56.900
In her study, as usual.

10:11.710 --> 10:13.830
Well, well, she's back.

10:13.830 --> 10:15.510
Who's she again?

10:15.510 --> 10:20.020
Some slob who wastes her time going 
to a worthless so-called College.

10:21.110 --> 10:23.260
Grandmother is calling.

10:23.260 --> 10:24.590
Pardon me.

10:26.470 --> 10:28.370
"Grandmother," she says.

10:28.370 --> 10:31.850
As if she sees her as her grandchild.

10:31.850 --> 10:35.010
She's the child of a woman 
who stole the succession.

10:39.980 --> 10:41.010
Alcyone.

10:42.740 --> 10:43.870
I'm here.

10:46.370 --> 10:50.720
A new student at the College caught 
onto me while I was concealed.

10:51.440 --> 10:52.740
Well.

10:53.250 --> 10:59.000
But we're capable of erasing almost 
all of our odors and magic scent.

10:59.490 --> 11:01.920
And yet I was noticed.

11:02.490 --> 11:05.750
Is this new student a student of sorcery?

11:06.150 --> 11:07.020
No.

11:07.920 --> 11:09.910
She seems to be a mage.

11:09.910 --> 11:11.830
Why is a mage there?

11:11.830 --> 11:13.560
I don't know what her goals are.

11:14.070 --> 11:16.660
She has a dog familiar.

11:16.660 --> 11:19.010
That may be why she was able to notice us.

11:19.650 --> 11:24.200
In that case, it wouldn't have 
been your aura, odor,

11:24.200 --> 11:26.430
or magic scent that she'd picked up.

11:26.800 --> 11:27.680
What, then?

11:28.290 --> 11:30.810
I've heard that mages and witches

11:30.810 --> 11:36.680
that are close to that world 
are sensitive to <i>the scent</i>.

11:36.680 --> 11:37.700
The scent?

11:38.160 --> 11:41.490
The scents of certain emotions,

11:41.490 --> 11:46.570
their changes and transitions, 
or even their very presence...

11:46.990 --> 11:50.050
Some say it's the smell of the soul itself.

11:50.940 --> 11:52.720
What shall I do?

11:53.700 --> 11:55.520
I'll think of something.

11:55.520 --> 11:57.070
Please give me some time.

11:57.840 --> 11:58.640
Okay.

12:11.130 --> 12:12.330
Come in.

12:16.120 --> 12:17.760
You're late.

12:18.900 --> 12:21.920
I apologize, Grandmother.

12:22.820 --> 12:26.110
Is Miss Veronica still well?

12:26.970 --> 12:27.720
Yes.

12:28.250 --> 12:32.000
We had no intention of 
sending you to the College.

12:32.000 --> 12:35.140
You are only permitted 
to attend by her charity.

12:35.580 --> 12:38.040
Do not embarrass me.

12:38.450 --> 12:39.160
Yes.

12:39.420 --> 12:42.410
Are you keeping up with your studies?

12:42.410 --> 12:43.160
Yes.

12:43.440 --> 12:46.380
You have no need for such an education,

12:46.380 --> 12:48.510
but as you are receiving it, 
you mustn't be negligent.

12:49.060 --> 12:49.650
Yes.

12:50.030 --> 12:54.030
We have no need for a follower 
who only knows how to say "yes."

12:55.210 --> 12:56.900
I'm sorry.

12:57.810 --> 13:01.050
You look as pale as ever.

13:01.050 --> 13:03.800
Are you taking proper care of your health?

13:04.580 --> 13:08.620
And here I was, about to 
give you a gift today.

13:12.750 --> 13:16.100
I never said you could raise your head.

13:16.100 --> 13:17.660
Greedy child.

13:18.120 --> 13:22.100
Do not anger me with your ineptitude.

13:24.420 --> 13:26.030
I'm sorry.

13:26.480 --> 13:28.390
Never mind.

13:28.390 --> 13:32.500
It's not as though you've 
ever been any better.

13:33.950 --> 13:35.880
Sit down over there.

13:36.400 --> 13:41.010
I trust that you remember why 
I called you home today.

13:42.250 --> 13:43.140
Yes.

14:10.450 --> 14:11.240
Damn.

14:11.630 --> 14:13.210
Swayne.

14:13.760 --> 14:15.330
I see you're working hard.

14:15.330 --> 14:16.410
Can I help you?

14:16.410 --> 14:20.530
I've never seen you so focused.

14:20.530 --> 14:21.640
What's changed?

14:21.640 --> 14:23.870
Nothing's changed, sir.

14:23.870 --> 14:27.170
At least tell a more convincing lie.

14:28.260 --> 14:31.770
You've been booking a lot of 
time in the training area.

14:31.770 --> 14:34.480
I heard you haven't been 
skipping classes, either.

14:34.900 --> 14:38.380
And you're using your dorm room again 
even though you left once already.

14:39.720 --> 14:43.100
Oh, I'm not admonishing you or anything!

14:43.340 --> 14:47.040
I mean, one of the College's
functions is to train protectors.

14:47.040 --> 14:49.620
There's nothing wrong with that.

14:49.620 --> 14:52.290
So what do you want from me, then?

14:52.630 --> 14:58.120
Everything's fine, but it's always the keen 
ones that end up taking it too far.

14:59.280 --> 15:00.770
Just look at me.

15:00.770 --> 15:02.260
I couldn't help myself.

15:02.260 --> 15:07.090
I couldn't help but keep working on 
my experiments, and now look at me.

15:07.600 --> 15:13.600
I was conscious when my skin came 
apart and melted and fused...

15:13.600 --> 15:15.770
It was pretty traumatic!

15:16.530 --> 15:19.730
It's only now that partial transfiguration, 
transformations, burns,

15:19.730 --> 15:22.080
and injuries are something to be proud of.

15:22.990 --> 15:27.560
But I used to get laughed at before, 
and it's not exactly convenient.

15:27.890 --> 15:30.330
I have to hide from people all the time.

15:32.220 --> 15:35.300
I suppose you're too young 
to care about any of that.

15:36.100 --> 15:37.280
It's just that...

15:37.970 --> 15:40.440
Someone said something
 I really didn't want to hear.

15:40.440 --> 15:43.090
So I wanna impress 'em.

15:47.450 --> 15:50.510
You can go ahead and increase 
your ammo and target cap.

15:50.510 --> 15:53.220
I'll take care of the budget for you.

15:54.390 --> 15:55.910
Thanks a ton!

15:58.070 --> 15:59.280
Ah, sure.

15:59.650 --> 16:01.590
The ammo and target cap, right?

16:01.590 --> 16:02.610
No problem.

16:02.610 --> 16:04.920
We can handle that.

16:05.270 --> 16:07.910
We have plenty of far more 
unreasonable requests.

16:09.700 --> 16:10.630
Yes.

16:10.630 --> 16:11.790
Bye.

16:19.040 --> 16:21.470
Something must have happened.

16:22.320 --> 16:25.910
You haven't started venting at all, 
even though you've got a drink ready.

16:27.330 --> 16:29.640
I'm not in the mood today.

16:29.640 --> 16:33.840
You're always in the mood 
to vent when you're here.

16:42.430 --> 16:45.380
You sure have grown.

16:45.380 --> 16:46.940
Or grown old, rather.

16:46.940 --> 16:50.850
Even a baby will be ready to 
drink after twenty years.

16:51.260 --> 16:54.350
I made a mistake, teaching 
you to love alcohol.

16:55.060 --> 16:59.600
You were the one who brought 
me a bottle for my graduation.

16:59.600 --> 17:04.510
I never would have let you take a sip if 
I'd known you'd be such a nasty drunk.

17:08.230 --> 17:09.290
I...

17:13.160 --> 17:18.350
I want her to stay a child 
until the time comes.

17:19.180 --> 17:21.130
She's 18 now.

17:21.630 --> 17:23.770
She's too old for me to be ordering around.

17:24.180 --> 17:26.610
It's up to her to decide her own future.

17:26.980 --> 17:28.210
But I...

17:29.760 --> 17:33.560
I don't want Alice to end 
up like me or my dad.

17:37.530 --> 17:39.480
Whenever there was
 something we wanted to do,

17:40.040 --> 17:43.860
we couldn't wait to become 
grown-ups, remember?

17:44.640 --> 17:49.590
And when we finally get older, 
we think we're finally grown-ups.

17:49.590 --> 17:53.010
But do you think we've 
actually become grown-ups?

17:53.010 --> 17:54.200
What's your point?

17:54.890 --> 18:00.320
Maybe what a kid wants to do and what a 
grown-up wants to do aren't all that different.

18:01.110 --> 18:07.230
You must know that girl's been 
desperate to make herself useful to you.

18:11.210 --> 18:12.410
That's the problem.

18:13.070 --> 18:17.270
<i>He's got to know that she's just going to 
resist if he tries to push her away.</i>

18:17.710 --> 18:20.410
<i>I guess emotions don't 
always agree with logic.</i>

18:20.740 --> 18:25.700
Sheesh, I never knew my 
senior was such a pain.

18:26.100 --> 18:29.040
You're more of an
 upperclassman in every way.

18:29.040 --> 18:30.500
No way.

18:30.500 --> 18:35.040
You graduated first, and you're 
the first one leaving.

18:35.040 --> 18:37.480
I'm the junior. That's how it ought to be.

18:37.930 --> 18:41.400
Some oddball junior you are.

18:41.920 --> 18:46.060
Nothing in life's ever gone my way.

18:46.060 --> 18:48.910
At least let me have this.

18:54.620 --> 18:59.060
Jeez, I wish I could get drunk on so little.

19:00.870 --> 19:04.600
I feel like I've been taking care 
of kids all the time lately.

19:07.690 --> 19:10.890
I should head home for once.

19:11.370 --> 19:13.110
Use my paid leave.

19:31.100 --> 19:32.470
Bushcraft?

19:32.470 --> 19:33.660
Yup.

19:33.660 --> 19:34.610
What's that?

19:34.950 --> 19:36.850
It's like camping.

19:36.850 --> 19:39.940
You learn the skills you 
need to live in nature.

19:40.580 --> 19:43.710
You don't know what's 
going to happen, or when.

19:44.260 --> 19:48.260
So you get yourself ready 
for whatever happens.

19:48.910 --> 19:56.830
As vessels of the knowledge of sorcery, 
our biggest priority is to survive.

19:56.830 --> 19:58.870
And cooking is part of that, too.

19:58.870 --> 20:03.000
So you learn to camp without using sorcery.

20:03.400 --> 20:04.630
It's fun.

20:04.630 --> 20:05.890
You switched tasks?

20:06.250 --> 20:08.670
I can never tell how gentle 
I need to be with the peeler.

20:09.510 --> 20:11.610
Where are we headed this year, again?

20:11.610 --> 20:13.280
Scotland, apparently.

20:13.280 --> 20:15.830
Man, it's so cold out there.

20:15.830 --> 20:18.370
You hate the cold, don't you, Martin?

20:18.840 --> 20:20.150
<i>Camping...</i>

20:20.520 --> 20:23.560
Okay, everyone, pair up!

20:24.610 --> 20:27.710
<i>I'm having flashbacks to my elementary 
and middle school field trips.</i>

20:28.060 --> 20:29.590
<i>No, it'll be fine.</i>

20:29.590 --> 20:31.680
<i>No one's like that here.</i>

20:32.110 --> 20:35.120
<i>And I've changed a bit, too.</i>

20:37.870 --> 20:41.180
It can come in handy, I guess.

20:42.540 --> 20:44.970
<i>I'll try looking forward to it.</i>

20:46.280 --> 20:49.170
<i>Scotland, though...</i>

20:49.170 --> 20:52.610
<i>I have a feeling Elias is going 
insist on coming along.</i>

20:57.100 --> 20:58.280
Oh?

21:16.920 --> 21:18.130
Listen up!

21:18.420 --> 21:20.710
This is going to be our campground.

21:21.400 --> 21:24.810
Split up and work with your groups.

21:24.810 --> 21:28.050
Securing your sleeping area, 
maintaining your fire, acquiring water...

21:28.320 --> 21:31.270
Those are your top priorities.

21:31.270 --> 21:32.700
Yes, sir.

21:36.630 --> 21:38.170
We can cut it up and eat it.

21:38.170 --> 21:40.220
But we brought food!

21:40.220 --> 21:42.000
I think I'm good for now.

21:42.000 --> 21:42.910
For <i>now</i>?!

21:43.250 --> 21:45.080
Can I have it, then?

21:45.080 --> 21:47.690
I'm not eating that, Beatrice!

21:53.610 --> 21:56.900
I didn't think there were any 
forests until we got here.

21:57.210 --> 21:58.750
I was wrong, huh?

21:59.210 --> 22:00.760
How are you not tired?

22:00.760 --> 22:04.640
Our groupmates are almost 
the same as our roommates.

22:04.640 --> 22:05.800
I look forward to it.

22:05.800 --> 22:07.460
Sure, whatever.

22:07.790 --> 22:12.830
All right, let's find wood for fuel 
and setting up our tent.

22:12.830 --> 22:13.560
Okay.
